WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.760 --> 00:00:07.010
Utqiaġvik, in northern Alaska, gets about
137 millimetres of precipitation a year.

2
00:00:07.060 --> 00:00:10.350
Phoenix, Arizona, gets about 183.

3
00:00:10.400 --> 00:00:12.090
Both are dry.

4
00:00:12.140 --> 00:00:15.370
Yet one is tundra, and
the other is hot desert.

5
00:00:15.420 --> 00:00:17.390
They look nothing alike.

6
00:00:17.440 --> 00:00:22.030
One widely used map divides
Earth's land into 14 biomes.

7
00:00:22.080 --> 00:00:23.330
So what sorts them?

8
00:00:23.380 --> 00:00:24.590
Rainfall alone?

9
00:00:24.640 --> 00:00:25.750
Soil?

10
00:00:25.800 --> 00:00:26.990
Distance from the sea?

11
00:00:27.040 --> 00:00:30.730
In this mission, you'll read
climate graphs for four places,

12
00:00:30.780 --> 00:00:32.850
from Alaska to Hawaii.

13
00:00:32.900 --> 00:00:35.610
Then you'll map where tundra, rainforest,

14
00:00:35.660 --> 00:00:39.090
hot desert and temperate
grassland lie on Earth.

15
00:00:39.140 --> 00:00:42.680
Your mission: find out what
sorts the world's biomes.
